# f-string

> Python f-string syntax and formatting options.
> More information: <https://fstring.help/cheat>.

- Print expression value and raw code (debugging):
  `f"{expression=}"`

- Format a float to a specific number of decimal places:
  `f"{number:.2f}"`

- Format a number with thousand separators:
  `f"{number:,}"`

- Left, right, or center align a string within a specific width:
  `f"{string:<20}"`
  `f"{string:>20}"`
  `f"{string:^20}"`

- Pad an integer or string with leading zeros:
  `f"{number:04d}"`
  `f"{string:0>10}"`

- Format an integer as binary, lowercase hex, or uppercase hex:
  `f"{number:b}"`
  `f"{number:x}"`
  `f"{number:X}"`

- Format a number as a percentage:
  `f"{percent:.0%}"`

- Force string representation (`str()`), repr (`repr()`), or ASCII-escaped repr (`ascii()`):
  `f"{expression!s}"`
  `f"{expression!r}"`
  `f"{expression!a}"`
